    "declared_proposition": "Fix M. Let R(n)=P_r(n) on each odd residue r mod M, with real polynomials P_r, and suppose R is bounded below on positive odd integers. Then R(T(n))<R(n) cannot hold on every accelerated Collatz edge.",
    "mathematical_argument": "Use n=4Mk-1 and T(n)=6Mk-1 in the same residue -1 mod M. A polynomial P_(-1) bounded below along the positive ray is constant or has positive leading coefficient. In the first case the rank difference is zero; in the second, P(6Mk-1)-P(4Mk-1) has positive leading coefficient a_d M^d(6^d-4^d), so it is positive for all sufficiently large k.",
